A||N||4||grinthock||valve stem locks?||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||12-13-2001||11:57 PM||||I have a problem.<P>The area where is live has some little shits who keep letting the air out of my tires, I can't put a prox alarm on it, it goes off when people walk their dog down the sidewalk, they finally popped the bead right out on the tire and now my car is STUCK...<P>It's happening OVER AND OVER and I can't catch the sh1t that's doing it, I would rather not catch him cause I would probably KILL the kid.<P>Do valve stem locks exist or can I do something to combat this?<P><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-14-2001||08:01 AM||||The best thing you can do is first install the all metal stems so they cant break them. they have metak caps that have a little box wrench with the set so you can tighten them down. Most people wont be carrying pliers with them. That about all you can do. Too bad they dont make the valve stem holes on the inside of the rim.||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||12-14-2001||08:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>The best thing you can do is first install the all metal stems so they cant break them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gee, can  a tazer device be connected to the stems  ?? ha ha<P>I'd try and set up a video camera somewhere, to catch them.<P>Leave the camera on, and connected to VCR & set for 2 am - 6 am<P>If the little jerks come by, you'd have them on video. Then take action<P>Good luck||||reg||6
Z||000003||grinthock||12-15-2001||12:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>The best thing you can do is first install the all metal stems so they cant break them. they have metak caps that have a little box wrench with the set so you can tighten them down. Most people wont be carrying pliers with them. That about all you can do. Too bad they dont make the valve stem holes on the inside of the rim.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>PERFECT!!  Anyone know where I can get these?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-15-2001||12:54 AM||||actually, metal stems are usually brass. they can be snapped off.<P>you can get metal stems at most parts/tire stores. use the shortest ones you can get to make them harder to break. put the caps on with a wrench or pliers.<P>You said the bead dropped off. rather unusual unless you tried to drive on a flat.<P>What makes you so certain someone is letting the air out? are the valve caps off after you replaced them? It's not uncommon to have multiple tires with "legitimate" leaks. Even if someone let them down once, if the beads didn't seal good then they will keep going down.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
